<title>RUSSIA: Russian MinFins ease in thin trading.</title>
<headline>Russian MinFins ease in thin trading.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices of Russian MinFin bonds eased further in thin trading on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>		 tranche  Dec 19		  Dec 18</p>
<p> 1999 maturity (3)    83.30-83.60	   83.40-83.75</p>
<p> 2003 maturity (4)    59.15-59.25	   59.45-59.60</p>
<p> 2008 maturity (5)    41.15-41.30	   41.60-41.95</p>
<p> 2006 maturity (6)    47.00-47.30	   47.40-47.75</p>
<p> 2011 maturity (7)    34.90-35.20	   35.40-35.65</p>
<p>&quot;Prices went down but there is hardly any trading,&quot; an International Moscow Bank dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said some banks, mainly Western ones, were seen quoting through brokers, while the rest had already closed their books for the holiday season.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
